{
  "mn12:0.1": "Middle Discourses 12 ",
  "mn12:0.2": "The Longer Discourse on the Lion’s Roar ",
  "mn12:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn12:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying outside the city of Vesālī in a woodland grove west of the town. ",
  "mn12:2.1": "Now at that time Sunakkhatta the Licchavi had recently left this teaching and training. ",
  "mn12:2.2": "He was telling a crowd in Vesālī: ",
  "mn12:2.3": "“The ascetic Gotama has no superhuman distinction in knowledge and vision worthy of the noble ones. ",
  "mn12:2.4": "He teaches what he’s worked out by logic, following a line of inquiry, expressing his own perspective. ",
  "mn12:2.5": "Regardless of his goal in teaching the Dhamma, it delivers one who applies it to the complete ending of suffering.” ",
  "mn12:3.1": "Then Venerable Sāriputta robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Vesālī for alms. ",
  "mn12:3.2": "He heard what Sunakkhatta was saying. ",
  "mn12:3.3": "",
  "mn12:3.4": "",
  "mn12:3.5": "",
  "mn12:3.6": "Then he wandered for alms in Vesālī. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and told him what had happened. ",
  "mn12:3.7": "",
  "mn12:3.8": "",
  "mn12:3.9": "",
  "mn12:3.10": "",
  "mn12:3.11": "",
  "mn12:4.1": "“Sāriputta, Sunakkhatta, that futile man, is angry. ",
  "mn12:4.2": "His words are spoken out of anger. ",
  "mn12:4.3": "Thinking he criticizes the Realized One, in fact he just praises him. ",
  "mn12:4.4"